  "Discr-1672-XXXX": {
    "id": "Discr-1672-XXXX",
    "name": "The Family and Medical Leave Act of 1993",
    "category": "Discrimination",
    "description": "Entitles eligible employees of covered employers to take unpaid, job-protected leave for specified family and medical reasons with continuation of group health insurance coverage under the same terms and conditions as if the employee had not taken leave.\n\n \tThe University must permit a \"spouse, son, daughter, parent, or next of kin\" to take up to 26 workweeks of leave to care for a member of the Armed Forces, including a member of the National Guard or Reserves, who is undergoing medical treatment, recuperation, or therapy, is otherwise in outpatient status, or is otherwise on the temporary disability retired list, for a serious injury or illness.",
